abstract: Ying ji li guo xin chu zhong dou qi shu (𠸄咭唎國新出種痘奇書; Bodleian Libraries, Oxford, Sinica 1417)
  is a Chinese vaccination pamphlet catalogued as an 1858 [Hong Kong] reprint edited by Wilhelm Lobscheid.
  It discusses the introduction and circulation of a Western vaccination practice and includes historical
  explanations, instrument and lesion illustrations with textual labels, and publication statements. It
  provides source material for research on late Qing medical publishing, medical translation, and Hong
  Kong printing history. This version first supplies an image-based initial transcription of the witness’s
  14 main original printed text faces, with later library inscriptions and unattributed folded-edge fragments
  distinguished, in source-linked JSON, TXT, and TEI XML. AI-assisted readings and image gaps are marked;
  the text has not undergone full human collation or subject-specialist review.
